            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous fulminant gangrene of distal colon and rectum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>174-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of a young female is reported who presented with acute abdomen and peritonitis. Emergency laparotomy revealed fulminant gangrene of descending colon and upper third of rectum. Two-stage procedure was carried out as transverse colostomy and subsequent colorectal anastomosis two months later.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
